## What the take-on tests assert on the real database

- receivable/payable net movement = total - amountPaid; default_revenue, default_expense,
  vat_output and vat_input net movement exactly 0; every entry exactly two lines and balanced.
- A fully paid document: zero journal lines, status `paid`, gl_journal_entry_id null.
- arSubLedgerCheck and apSubLedgerCheck both `pass` after a mixed file of part-paid, unpaid
  and fully paid documents. Under the previous shape both failed.
- getVATReturn over the period: every box amount, every transaction list, both totals and
  netVAT byte-identical before and after an import. standardRatedSupplies and
  standardRatedPurchases DO move (+1000 each) because they are read from the invoice tables,
  not the GL — asserted explicitly rather than left to be discovered.
- R-002 boundary: 0.01 imports with a warning, 0.50 is refused naming all three amounts.
- R-020: a trial balance carrying a receivable or a payable control line is refused and
  writes nothing; the clearing residual is recorded on the session at completeSession, and
  not recorded when take-on and the trial balance agree.

