FIXTURE CONTAMINATION (R-036) — how the H2 test avoids it
  The fixture DB carries uq_supplier_invoices_supplier_number, K-107's migration
  646, which is on no origin ref and NOT in production. It raises 23505 on the
  corrected re-run and would mask the defect completely. The three new AP tests
  run `DROP INDEX IF EXISTS uq_supplier_invoices_supplier_number` INSIDE their
  own transaction and assert it is gone from pg_indexes before importing; DDL is
  transactional in Postgres, so the ROLLBACK in `finally` restores it and no
  other worktree's run is affected. Verified: with the index present and the
  production change reverted the corrected re-run raises "duplicate key value
  violates unique constraint"; with it dropped it silently imports a SECOND row.

